  [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/). ### Format ```
  <type
    >(<scope
      >):
      <subject>
        ``` ### Types - `feat` — New feature - `fix` — Bug fix - `docs` — Documentation changes -
        `refactor` — Code refactor (no feature or fix) - `test` — Adding or updating tests - `chore`
        — Maintenance, dependencies, configuration ### Examples ``` feat(core): add retry logic
        fix(parser): handle empty input docs(readme): update usage examples test(core): add edge
        case tests ``` --- ## Pull Requests 1. Fork the repository and create your branch from
        `main`. 2. Make your changes. 3. Ensure tests pass: `{{commands.test}}` 4. Submit a pull
        request.
